.TH elfshaker-esi-remove 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-esi\-remove \- Remove pack URLs from one or more remote indexes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker esi remove\fR [OPTIONS] <ESI_FILE> <PACK_URL>...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove entries whose stored URL exactly matches each PACK_URL from ESI_FILE and every index named by \-\-also. A missing URL is an error unless \-\-force is present. All targets are validated before any target changes, and changed indexes are backed up unless \-\-no\-backup is present.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Ignore stored URLs that are not present.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-backup\fR
Do not write .bak copies of the previous index contents.
.TP
\fB\-\-also\fR \fI<ESI_FILE>\fR
Apply the same operation to another ESI file; may be repeated.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIESI_FILE\fR>
Primary ESI file to edit.
.TP
<\fIPACK_URL\fR>...
Stored pack URLs to remove.
.SH EXAMPLES
Remove the stored release.pack URL from a v1 compatibility index and a v2 index:
.PP
.nf
\fBelfshaker esi remove \-\-also index.esi index.v2.esi release.pack\fR
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
elfshaker\-esi(1), elfshaker\-esi\-list(1), elfshaker\-esi\-add(1)
